  "content": {
    "id": "v2-c-p54-applications-slot-9-upper-root",
    "type": "question",
    "label": null,
    "prompt": "The height, $h$ metres, of a basketball above the court when it is $x$ metres horizontally from the shooter is given by $h=-0.5x^2+2x+2$. Find the horizontal distances at which the ball is 3 metres above the court. Give your answers to 2 decimal places.",
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [],
    "answer": {
      "short": "$x\\approx0.59$ m or $x\\approx3.41$ m.",
      "worked": "Let $h=3$.\n$$\\begin{align*}-0.5x^2+2x+2&=3\\\\-0.5x^2+2x-1&=0\\\\x^2-4x+2&=0\\\\x&=\\frac{-(-4)\\pm\\sqrt{(-4)^2-4(1)(2)}}{2(1)}\\\\x&=\\frac{4\\pm\\sqrt8}{2}\\\\x&=2\\pm\\sqrt2\\\\x&\\approx0.59\\text{ or }3.41\\end{align*}$$\nThe ball is 3 m high at about 0.59 m and 3.41 m from the shooter.",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
    "answerSpaceMm": null
  },
